WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.490
Chris Gore, Founder/Owner of FilmThreat/Author/Filmmaker:
Please, if you are a studio executive and

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:05.529
you’re watching this, do not ruin Back To
The Future.

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:09.280
Do not ruin Back To The Future by making a
female Back To The Future.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.970
It would be terrible.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.150
Think about it deeply.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.850
This is not a good idea.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:24.869
Seek out original ideas from original creators
who have original stories to tell…please…please.

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:35.660
Film Courage: Chris we asked you previously
why 99% of today’s movies are garbage.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.600
That was a few months ago where I asked you
that question.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.850
The video has got well over 5,000 comments,
a lot of people have opinions about it.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.470
Upon reflection is there anything you’d
like to add or clarify that you didn’t with

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.810
that video?

00:00:49.810 --> 00:01:00.050
Chris: Well…I mean…that could be an ongoing
podcast why 99% of movies are garbage.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:06.320
It’s really documenting all of the mistakes
filmmakers make.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.900
I think one that I’ve seen as a trend that
I think I failed to mention in previous video

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.070
was the gender swapping of characters.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:23.510
I think that…I mean I’ve seen how people
think that that’s…well we will just do

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.430
a female Terminator.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:30.440
Or we will just do a female version of x.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:38.960
I always think it’s better to start with
an original character and approach a film

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.660
that way.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:45.210
I find it kind of pandering on Hollywood’s
part to be like where are just going to do

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:51.140
this franchise which we already know is proven
success and we are going to gender-swap the

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:58.080
lead, I think that’s lazy, I think it’s
pandering to a certain audience.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:05.070
The audience may not even really be there
and I think that fans of those franchises

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:11.310
completely see through that.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:20.270
I mean the latest that Mad Max movie that
they did recently Fury Road he is really kind

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:28.730
of the side character but what Charlize Theron
did she created this amazing new character

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.900
that was kind of the right way of doing that.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:40.670
The wrong way might have been the Terminator
film Dark Fate which I’m not sure who loved

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.160
that movie.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:50.900
I know it did not do too well at the box office
Sarah Connor is already an amazing character.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:57.970
I don’t know why you need to flip things
and gender swap.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.230
Again I think audiences see through that.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:09.330
And example (we talked about this earlier)
is one that thankfully they will hopefully

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:13.020
never do which is Back To The Future.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.489
There have been rumblings of bringing the
Back To The Future franchise and doing a reboot

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:19.489
of Back To The Future.

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:24.489
There was a rumor a couple of years ago (and
I pay very little attention to rumors) because

00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:29.440
most of them we all know are bull but there
was a strong rumor that Justin Bieber was

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:36.599
going to be in a reboot of the Back To The
Future series but that franchise I don’t

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:48.209
think you could ever gender swap the lead
and call that lead Mandy McFly and having

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:55.160
some sort of weird relationship with a younger
version of her father would be very awkward.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.270
That just doesn’t work.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:00.019
And then there are cases where gender swapping
is irrelevant.

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:08.230
For example the upcoming Dune movie with Timothée
Chalamet, there is a character called Dr.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:14.940
Liet-Kynes which I’ve read the novel and
obviously seen the 1984 David Lynch film.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.979
The gender of that character is absolutely
irrelevant, not relevant to the character

00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:24.309
whatsoever in that case.

00:04:24.309 --> 00:04:27.490
Maybe in some ways can kind of add to something.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:33.770
When you are doing it just to pander it to
an audience, audiences can see through it.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:41.830
I really feel that when you are pandering
whether it’s queer baiting or gender swapping

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:47.240
characters or race swapping, it’s lazy,
it’s lazy.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:05:01.490
I’d rather see more original characters
that are maybe by female creators, black creators.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:02.490
Where are their voices?

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:07.430
If you are simply taking creators who have
done things and just changing the gender or

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:19.270
race I find is lazy and I think that audiences
they are not really in favor of that.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:28.319
It seems to not be working and I think if
Hollywood just leaned a little bit into originality,

00:05:28.319 --> 00:05:36.629
a little bit more into originality and took
some risks with new creators.

00:05:36.629 --> 00:05:40.729
See that’s the thing that I think people
don’t understand is that the original creators

00:05:40.729 --> 00:05:48.800
of those characters, they get money and so
I don’t understand why there is not more

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:58.279
of an effort to find people who have created
original characters that are all across the

00:05:58.279 --> 00:06:04.909
spectrum of ethnicity or gender and make movies
with this characters.

00:06:04.909 --> 00:06:15.430
I mean the original creators of those properties
would profit so I think pandering is probably

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:23.360
a huge mistake and under estimating in understanding
how savvy audiences are that they see through

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.360
it.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.900
Film Courage: So if I come in and say I want
to do a male version of Heathers or Jennifer’s

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:36.240
Body or Mean Girls…there is male bullying,
there’s all sorts of stuff.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.899
So it’s John’s Body, that’s not going
to work?

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:41.899
Chris: Sure.

00:06:41.899 --> 00:06:44.419
Film Courage: Or it’s so blatant that I’m
flipping it.

00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:46.439
Chris: Here’s the thing, I’ve seen that
story.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:48.759
I’ve seen those stories.

00:06:48.759 --> 00:06:53.759
Changing the gender is not going to…make
me care about the character because the point

00:06:53.759 --> 00:07:04.520
is is this, I identify with so many characters
that aren’t me and I think you have to create

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.939
something that comes from the essence of what
that character is.

00:07:06.939 --> 00:07:14.379
Ripley is a character I loved as a kid, Ellen
Ripley [Alien] played beautifully by Sigourney

00:07:14.379 --> 00:07:26.550
Weaver in two and a half good movies but I
think that just the the sort of I think it's

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:31.719
just lazy to do that but it's an opportunity
for an audience to identify with someone that

00:07:31.719 --> 00:07:39.379
isn't them and I feel like you have to as
an audience member be capable of seeing the

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:41.229
world through someone else's eyes.

00:07:41.229 --> 00:07:48.180
I've said this before I don't know if I've
said it in another video but you have to as

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.810
an audience member have the ability to identify
with someone who's not you.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:58.509
That's how you know even the storytelling
is great if you can take just sort of a regular

00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:06.419
dude like me and I can identify with a woman
who's maybe not a woman who's white, so maybe

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:11.959
not a woman from the United States, who's
maybe a woman that's going…that to me is

00:08:11.959 --> 00:08:14.439
great storytelling.

00:08:14.439 --> 00:08:21.749
I would say another film that I thoroughly
loved Amélie, French film Amélie right.

00:08:21.749 --> 00:08:26.569
Okay not a woman I don't speak French you
know a lot of her experience is very different

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:29.699
from mine but I identified with her.

00:08:29.699 --> 00:08:38.690
I was on her journey and so that to me is
storytelling is great when you know vastly

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:44.390
different people can identify with someone
that is not themselves.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:50.350
I don't need to see me reflected in a film
in fact I prefer not to.

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:56.070
I want to see someone new and interesting
and different and I think that what's lacking

00:08:56.070 --> 00:09:04.960
in the storytelling is making these stories
universal so the gender and ethnicity is irrelevant.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.970
It should be irrelevant.

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:14.900
Film Courage: You had said earlier about the
Marty McFly character turning into Mandy Mcfly

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:20.630
and you're right, it wouldn't work for the
especially for the one fact of flipping it

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:25.620
with the dad now to have a Biff character
that's female that's bullying her that actually

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:30.200
would be interesting and then her sort of
going on this journey and playing in a band.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:34.430
Chris: See now you're being like a studio
executive and you're you're pitching the female

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:35.940
Back to the Future.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:42.660
Please, please, please…I will say this to
camera which I know my eye line is you but

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:46.400
I'm going to say to camera, please if you're
a studio executive you are watching this,

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.810
do not ruin Back to the Future.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:52.560
Do not ruin Back to the Future by making a
female Back to the Future.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:55.260
It would be terrible.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.450
Think about it deeply.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.140
This is not a good idea.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:12.080
Seek out original ideas from original creators
who have original stories to tell…please…please…so

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:15.680
I don't have to do a third version of this
video… please.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:16.570
Question for the Viewers: Anything you disagree
with?

